course: dictionary
lesson: 6486
title: Nay: old-fashioned no, and more
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Nay is an old word for «no». You will meet it in old stories and old Bible translations, where a character might say «nay» instead of «no». If someone is refusing something, the context tells you that nay is a no.
explain: Nay can also be a formal word that adds a stronger word to a point: «It was hard, nay, impossible.» The writer means it was not just hard, but even impossible. Test it by swapping in «not only that, but even» and see if the sentence still makes sense.
explain: As a noun, a nay is a no vote, as in «the ayes and the nays» when people vote in a meeting. A yes vote is an aye (or a yea), and a no vote is a nay. Phrases to know: «yea or nay» and «say nay».
fact: Nay means no, in old-fashioned English.
fact: «Nay» can add a stronger word to a point, as in «hard, nay, impossible».
fact: A nay is a no vote, and its plural is nays.
fact: «Let your yea be yea; and your nay, nay» is an old phrase from Bible translations.
fact: Nay sounds like the French word nez, which means nose, but they are different words.
exercise: «Nay, I will not come with you.» What does nay mean here? | Yes, of course | *No | Maybe later | Happy to go
exercise: «The task was hard, nay, impossible.» What extra job does nay do here? | *It adds a stronger word, so the task was even impossible | It is a number | It means the task was easy | It means the task was finished
exercise: In «the ayes and the nays», what is a nay? | *A no vote | A kind of bird | A shout of joy | A yes vote
test: «The king said nay to the plan.» What does said nay mean? | Said hello | Said yes | Said goodbye | *Said no
test: The meeting counted 12 ayes and 3 nays. How many people voted no? | 12 | *3 | 2 | 15
exam: «Say nay» is an old way of saying what? | Say it quietly | Say yes | *Say no | Say sorry
